<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
			if ( ! isset( $this->wp_locale_mapping[ $deepl_code ] ) ) {
				throw new Exception( "No WP locale mapping for DeepL code: {$deepl_code}" );
			}
			$wp_locale   = $this->wp_locale_mapping[ $deepl_code ];
			$output_file = $this->lang_dir . '/ultimate-multisite-' . $wp_locale . '.po';

			echo "Translating to {$language_name} ({$deepl_code} -> {$wp_locale})... ";

			// Skip if file exists and we're not forcing re-translation
			if ( file_exists( $output_file ) && ! $this->force ) {
				echo "SKIPPED (file exists, use --force to overwrite)\n";
				continue;
			}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In scripts/translate.php around lines 132 to 141, the code directly indexes
$this->wp_locale_mapping[$deepl_code] which can emit PHP notices if the mapping
is missing; before using it, check isset($this->wp_locale_mapping[$deepl_code])
(or array_key_exists) and if missing echo a clear error message including
$language_name and $deepl_code and then continue to the next language, otherwise
assign $wp_locale from the mapping and proceed to build $output_file; this
prevents notices and provides a clear diagnostic when mappings diverge.
```

</details>

