In `@tests/WP_Ultimo/Managers/Notes_Manager_Test.php` around lines 135 - 154, The
helper capture_json_response currently only calls ob_get_clean() and
remove_ajax_die_handler($handler) after the try/catch, so any exception other
than \WPAjaxDieContinueException will skip cleanup; wrap the callable invocation
and the catch logic in a try/finally (or add a finally) that always calls
ob_get_clean() and remove_ajax_die_handler($handler), preserving/rehrowing any
caught exception (or returning the captured output as before) so hooks and
output buffering are always unwound; update the function capture_json_response
to ensure cleanup runs in the finally and that the existing
\WPAjaxDieContinueException handling remains intact.
