_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Avoid shared global constants in tests; this can make results order/environment dependent.**

`TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY` / `TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET` are process-global and cannot be undefined. Once defined in one test (or pre-defined in environment), other setup tests can silently change behavior.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 class Provider_With_Constants extends Concrete_Test_Provider {
@@
 	public function __construct() {
@@
-		$this->id        = 'provider-with-constants';
-		$this->constants = ['TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY', 'TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET'];
+		$this->id        = 'provider-with-constants';
+		$this->constants = ['WU_TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY', 'WU_TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET'];
 	}
 }
@@
 	public function test_is_setup_returns_false_when_constant_missing(): void {
-
-		$provider = new Provider_With_Constants();
+		$provider = new Concrete_Test_Provider();
+		$provider->set_constants(['WU_TEST_MISSING_API_KEY', 'WU_TEST_MISSING_SECRET']);
@@
 	public function test_is_setup_returns_true_when_all_constants_defined(): void {
-
-		if (! defined('TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY')) {
-			define('TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY', 'test-key-value');
+		if (! defined('WU_TEST_SETUP_API_KEY')) {
+			define('WU_TEST_SETUP_API_KEY', 'test-key-value');
 		}

-		if (! defined('TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET')) {
-			define('TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET', 'test-secret-value');
+		if (! defined('WU_TEST_SETUP_SECRET')) {
+			define('WU_TEST_SETUP_SECRET', 'test-secret-value');
 		}

-		$provider = new Provider_With_Constants();
+		$provider = new Concrete_Test_Provider();
+		$provider->set_constants(['WU_TEST_SETUP_API_KEY', 'WU_TEST_SETUP_SECRET']);

 		$this->assertTrue($provider->is_setup());
 	}
```
</details>




Also applies to: 351-357, 362-375

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@tests/WP_Ultimo/Integrations/Host_Providers/Base_Host_Provider_Test.php`
around lines 133 - 138, The test constructor sets process-global constant names
via $this->constants (in __construct of the provider-with-constants test) which
creates shared global state across tests; change the approach to avoid global
constants by removing those global names from $this->constants and instead
inject test-specific credentials via the test instance or controlled environment
management: populate credentials in setUp() on the test object (or use
putenv/getenv with unique keys) and clean them in tearDown(), or generate unique
constant names per-test and define/undefine them within setUp()/tearDown();
update references to TEST_PROVIDER_API_KEY/TEST_PROVIDER_SECRET to read from the
instance properties or the controlled env accessor so no process-global
constants are relied upon.
```

</details>

