**Avoid unconditional pass paths in JSON endpoint tests.**

These branches let tests pass even when output is invalid/non-JSON (`assertTrue(true)`), which can mask regressions in handlers. Fail fast when decoding fails, and assert the expected response shape every time.



<details>
<summary>✅ Suggested hardening pattern</summary>

```diff
+	private function decode_json_response(string $output): array {
+		$decoded = json_decode($output, true);
+		$this->assertIsArray($decoded, 'Expected valid JSON response.');
+		$this->assertArrayHasKey('success', $decoded);
+		return $decoded;
+	}
